.TH BACKLIGHT-CTL 1 "January 2025" "backlight-ctl 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
backlight-ctl \- keyboard backlight control daemon and utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B backlight-ctl
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B backlight-ctl
is a utility for controlling keyboard backlight on laptops with automatic activity detection. It can run as a daemon to automatically manage backlight based on keyboard and touchpad activity, with different timeouts for battery and AC power.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon [--debug]
Run as background daemon. Use --debug for verbose output.
.TP
.BI "set " LEVEL
Set backlight level immediately. LEVEL must be 0 (off), 1 (low), or 2 (high).
.TP
.B get
Display current backlight level.
.TP
.B status
Show detailed status including power source, timeouts, and current settings.
.TP
.B enable
Enable automatic backlight control.
.TP
.B disable
Disable automatic backlight control.
.TP
.BI "config " KEY " " VALUE
Configure daemon settings. Valid keys:
.RS
.TP
.B battery_timeout
Timeout in seconds when on battery power (5-300).
.TP
.B ac_timeout
Timeout in seconds when on AC power (10-600).
.TP
.B ac_default_level
Default backlight level on AC power (0-2).
.TP
.B battery_default_level
Default backlight level on battery power (0-2).
.RE
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Activity Detection
Monitors laptop keyboard and touchpad activity via i8042 interrupts. External USB devices are ignored.
.TP
.B Power-Aware Timeouts
Uses different timeout values for battery and AC power to optimize battery life.
.TP
.B Gradual Dimming
On AC power with level 2, gradually dims from 2→1→0 over the timeout period.
.TP
.B Configuration Persistence
Settings are saved to ~/.config/backlight-control.conf and automatically reloaded.
.SH GUI TOOLS
.TP
.B backlight-config
Zenity-based configuration wizard for setting timeouts and default levels.
.TP
.B backlight-control-panel
GUI control panel for manual backlight control and service management.
.TP
.B backlight-status-bar.sh
Status bar indicator showing current mode (⌨A for auto, ⌨M for manual) with click menu for quick access to controls.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/backlight-control.conf
User configuration file
.TP
.I /etc/backlight-control.conf
System-wide configuration file
.TP
.I /sys/class/leds/tpacpi::kbd_backlight/brightness
Kernel interface for backlight control (ThinkPad)
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/backlight-control.desktop
Desktop entry for GUI access (optional)
.SH SYSTEMD SERVICE
The daemon is typically run as a systemd service:
.PP
.nf
sudo systemctl enable backlight-control
sudo systemctl start backlight-control
.fi
.PP
The service automatically starts on boot and reloads configuration when changed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Set backlight to maximum:
.B backlight-ctl set 2
.TP
Configure 45-second timeout on battery:
.B backlight-ctl config battery_timeout 45
.TP
Run daemon with debug output:
.B backlight-ctl daemon --debug
.TP
Check current status:
.B backlight-ctl status
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments or configuration error
.SH SIGNALS
When running as daemon:
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Reload configuration from file
.TP
.B SIGTERM, SIGINT
Graceful shutdown
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.B Hardware
ThinkPad or compatible laptop with keyboard backlight
.TP
.B Permissions
Root access required for sysfs writes, or user in 'video' group with appropriate udev rules
.TP
.B Kernel
Linux with i8042 keyboard controller support
